## 2. Task Model – Tables

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|----------------------|
| **AT1 – Compute Collection Order** | Determine the optimal sequence of storages for collection. | – | *Control Center* | 1 |
| **AT2 – Send Resource Request** | Transmit the resource request message to the selected storage. | – | *Robot’s current location (storage)* | 1 |
| **AT3 – Wait for Retrieval** | Block until the storage confirms that resources have been retrieved. | – | *Robot’s current location (storage)* | 1 |
| **AT4 – Return to Recharge Station** | Move robot to the nearest charging station. | – | *Recharge Station* | 1 |
| **AT5 – Assign Mission to Another Robot** | Notify control centre to re‑assign the remaining collection task. | – | *Control Center* | 1 |
| **AT6 – Transport Resources to Destination** | Carry the collected resources from storage to the delivery destination. | – | *From Storage to Destination* | 1 |
| **AT7 – Check Delivery Completed** | Verify that all resources have arrived at the destination. | – | *Destination* | 1 |
| **AT8 – Return Resource to Checkpoint** | Move the partially delivered resource to a checkpoint. | – | *Checkpoint* | 1 |
| **AT9 – Assign Remaining Task** | Re‑assign the remaining delivery task to another robot. | – | *Control Center* | 1 |
| **AT10 – Send Alert on Failure** | Trigger an alert to the sector manager if the resource cannot be returned to the checkpoint. | – | *Control Center* | 1 |

