## 4. Logical Relationships

```
G1 -> G2, G3 [AND][sequential]
G2 -> G2.1, G2.4 [OR][parallel]
G2.1 -> G2.1.1, G2.1.2, G2.1.3 [AND][parallel]
G2.4 -> G2.4.1, G2.4.2 [AND][parallel]
G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [OR][parallel]
G3.1 -> G3.1.1, G3.1.2 [AND][parallel]
G3.2 -> G3.2.1, G3.2.2 [AND][parallel]
G3.2.2 -> G3.2.2.1, G3.2.2.2 [AND][parallel]

AT1 -> G2.1.1
AT2 -> G2.1.2
AT3 -> G2.1.3
AT4 -> G2.4.1
AT5 -> G2.4.2
AT6 -> G3.1.1
AT7 -> G3.1.2
AT8 -> G3.2.1
AT9 -> G3.2.2.1
AT10 -> G3.2.2.2
```

These relationships capture the hierarchical and parallel/sequence structure of the mission, mapping each goal to its constituent sub‑goals and each task to the leaf goal it implements.
